+### 1.5 Glossary — metrics used across the report (the "X" and "Z" of the falsifiers)
+
+- **Cross-office task:** a thread/issue/obligation where ≥ 2 offices are involved. **Cross-office root task:** work that passes through more than one office's authority without a formal owner.
+- **Owner lead time (LT):** median/mean of (owner's first action − task trigger) for tasks with a named owner; for baseline (no named owner), LT = time to first action by any office.
+- **Institutional delay (ID):** mean/median of **days** from cross-office request to terminal evidence (Act 18 §2 terminal state on the originating issue; in Git: days from trigger commit to terminal commit).
+- **Founder-visible frequency (FOV):** number of terminal/stage updates on Town Hall per cross-office task (per Act 18 §2; the Act 18 + Act 30 §7 digest machinery makes these visible).
+- **Owner-free time (OFT):** share of cross-office task time during which no named next-action owner exists (baseline = 100% of tasks; all cross-office tasks are unowned).
+- **Rework (RW):** tasks reopened after a terminal update or opened twice by different offices (re-derivation/rework of the same root task).
+- **Review coverage (RC):** fraction of terminal states carrying independent verification evidence (Act 21 §2 suite-status on the exact candidate; Act 23 §5.1 independent closure; Act 28 exact-tree attestation where applicable).
+- **Coordination overhead (OV):** extra messages/dispatches/tokens attributable to the new arrangement, measured per task.
