+## 4. Telemetry design — "routine ownership assignment" tool (H_C cost-benefit)
+
+- **Minimal version (the tool):** for each cross-office obligation, in the **originating thread or handoff**, name: **Owner** (one existing office), **next action**, **terminal evidence requirement**, **review point** (the H_C elevation; law-free via Act 30 §1 machinery; only the Owner status becomes standing).
+- **Telemetry design (telemetry-only, additive, reversible; requires no law):**
+  - Generated telemetry: generated additive records under `records/` (Act 31 §3.1: additive records land on green suite without review — precedent: Act 18 §7 generated `records/board-trail/index.json`). Suggested: a generated cross-office index (e.g., extend `records/tracking/` entries or generate `records/cross-office-tasks/` with task id, offices involved, owner, time-to-terminal-evidence, duplicates, rework, review coverage) + digest lines (Act 30 §7 digest already reports "passes with no change", "obligations expired", "days since each office last produced a durable result" — extend with cross-office metrics).
+  - Metrics to record:
+    - **Owner lead time per cross-office task** (median + fraction of tasks without a named owner — OFT).
+    - **Institutional delay** (ID: days trigger → terminal evidence).
+    - **Founder-visible frequency** (FOV: terminal updates per task — Act 18 §2).
+    - **Rework count** (RW: reopened/duplicated root tasks).
+    - **Review coverage** (RC: fraction of terminal updates with independent-verification evidence, Act 21/23).
+  - Proposal for telemetry-only changes (no law, reversible, measurable):
+    1. Write the elevation (Owner, next action, terminal evidence, review point, review date) in the originating thread — for a sample of cross-office tasks.
+    2. Add generated additive records (cross-office index/digest extension) — additive, reversible (delete).
+    3. Measure baseline (pre) vs elevated (post) per §3 Exp-1 metrics over the next windows.
+    4. If H_C does not improve ID or introduces RW without reducing OFT, revert (delete additive records; elevations recorded per task; owners free to change).
+    5. Nothing changes: offices, dispatch paths, law, standings (only "Owner" attribution, which was already true informally), or review paths.
+
