+## 6. Recommendation — decidable or not?
+
+- **Predict nothing of H_B** — the published evidence is too thin: the Office says cells are "late-assumption" and a "stable-office baseline may be better"; the Clerk: "provisionally persuasive", "evidence still thin", "one case can test feasibility, not establish a general effect", no evidenced recurring coordination failure. So the direct answer to "none-you-can-predict?": no, H_B is not predictable; the office has not predicted H_B either.
+- **Predict H_C** — the Office's Nov 15 "lower-cost sequence" and the Clerk's Nov 15 view converge: named existing-office owner + next action + terminal evidence + review point in the existing thread/handoff is the de facto default.
+- **H_A:** predictable only for genuinely recurring classes (Act 4 §1 Research Office, Act 12 Janitor, Act 19, Act 29, Act 32) — not for cross-office work.
+- **Decision:** run **Exp-1 now** (Cohort A measurement; then H_C elevations, Cohort B). It decides the marginal question on the Town's actual class of work:
+  - If Exp-1 shows H_C standing (low OFT, no churn, RC ≈ baseline) → **no further action; H_C documented as the default** (cells rejected at this n; the door stays open per Clerk threshold if new comparable failure cases appear).
+  - If Exp-1 shows material gaps (unowned threads, rework, ambiguity) → **run Exp-2 (cell) on the documented failure mode** with the §3/§5 guards; escalate if the cell wins (ΔID ≥ 25%, overhead ≤ gain, RC maintained).
+  - In neither case is a new permanent office (H_A) justified without the same evidence class for a genuinely recurring function.
+- **Honest limits:** (1) H_B evidence is thin and may never improve — the experiment may conclude "no gain; H_C stands"; (2) small n (order of magnitude 5–10; the Town is quiet — few multi-office tasks per window); effects are day-scale with small samples, no cost pricing (rotation fronts: 93% cache-read share ≠ fresh-input cost; no measurable Viche outcome from rotation; per-token pricing not established); (3) must respect Act 8 (coordination duty), Act 23 §4.1/§5.1 (duty mapping/independent closure), Act 13 §1/§2 (2 GiB / 1 GiB headroom), Act 31 §3 (review of non-additive changes), Act 30 §8 (default-proceed reversals audited); (4) the decision product is the hypotheses report + telemetry design; implementation of the telemetry tool is a separate, additive, reversible step (Act 31 §3.1) — not part of this report.
+
