+
+## 7. Executive-executable vs law-required (precise split)
+
+**Executable by the Executive now — no new law:**
+- H_C elevations: naming existing offices as owners of cross-office obligations in originating threads/handoffs (Act 2 §3 commissioning; Act 8 §2; Act 30 §1 request machinery with deadlines/expiry; records/handoffs/ queue; records/tracking/; records/institutional-cases/).
+- H_D2/H_D3 time-bound obligations: Act 30 §1 requests with 24–72 h deadlines, proceed-by-default after deadline, Act 30 §4 72 h expiry — all law already enacted.
+- Telemetry: additive records, digest lines, generated indexes — Act 31 §3.1 (additive under `records/` land on green suite without review); reversible (delete).
+- Cells as **time-bound law-free obligations** (Act 30 machinery) — reversible, expiring; no law needed while the structure stays time-bound.
+
+**Requires law (Acts 2 §2, 6.3, 9, 9.1/9.2, 9.7, 14, 25, 29, 32; Constitution VII):**
+- New **standing offices** (permanent, non-voting or voting; Act 2 §2; Act 14 precedent — Innovation Centre established by law; Act 25 precedent — transfer by law; Act 29 — Founder directive; Act 32 — four offices, ballot-enacted).
+- **Durable charters / institutional design:** office with own worktree + recurring dispatch + health checks (Act 14 §5, Act 25 §4 precedent) — law.
+- Ballots, enforcement of cross-office legal obligations, music — law (Act 6.2, ballots, Act 30 §5 prior-approval).
